WEBVTT

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.323
Did you know our

00:00:01.343 --> 00:00:03.230
SALARY CYCLE is changing?

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.339
Here's what it means for you.

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.647
Up to now, it has followed

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.860
a JANUARY-to-DECEMBER cycle

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.851
12 months, one cycle.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.282
MERIT

00:00:14.302 --> 00:00:18.250
Projected market salary movement

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.141
BONUS

00:00:19.161 --> 00:00:22.870
Estimated Company Performance KPIs

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.719
HSE  ·  FINANCE  ·  PERFORMANCE

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.470
Now, we're moving to a new cycle.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.904
From APRIL to MARCH

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.362
Merit increases and promotions

00:00:37.382 --> 00:00:39.420
take effect on APRIL 1

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.551
That's where the cycle now begins.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.103
BONUS

00:00:44.123 --> 00:00:47.010
paid in the MARCH payroll

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:48.840
MARCH is the last month

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.234
of the cycle

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.530
One thing that isn't changing

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.192
Your PERFORMANCE APPRAISAL

00:00:55.212 --> 00:00:56.920
stays on the same schedule

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.362
and it will still close

00:00:58.382 --> 00:00:59.682
in DECEMBER

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.000
One more thing worth knowing

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.320
Say your merit increase is 5%

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.928
The implementation year covers

00:01:09.948 --> 00:01:13.010
15 MONTHS instead of 12

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:16.564
5% ÷ 12 = about 0.417%

00:01:16.584 --> 00:01:18.230
per month

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.130
Multiply that by 15 months

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.747
and the equivalent becomes

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:25.067
6.25%

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:27.900
APRIL to MARCH

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.009
That's the one to remember.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.310
Why the change?

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.500
Closer to market best practice

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:37.598
More relevant information

00:01:37.618 --> 00:01:39.699
when we set salaries

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.970
If you have questions,

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.683
HR is ready to help.
